# Coding Style Guide

Quick reference for Laravel + Vue 3 coding style conventions.

## PHP/Laravel Style

### 1. Type Declarations (REQUIRED - PHP 8.2+)

```php
// ✅ CORRECT: Full type declarations
public function createMarket(array $data): Market
{
    return Market::create($data);
}

public function getUserById(int $id): ?User
{
    return User::find($id);
}

// ❌ WRONG: No types
public function createMarket($data)
{
    return Market::create($data);
}
```

### 2. Method Size (Keep Small)

```php
// ✅ CORRECT: Small, focused methods
public function store(StoreMarketRequest $request): RedirectResponse
{
    $market = $this->marketService->create($request->validated());
    return redirect()->route('markets.show', $market);
}

// ❌ WRONG: Fat controller (>50 lines)
public function store(Request $request)
{
    // 100 lines of validation, business logic, database operations
    // Extract to service layer!
}
```

### 3. Early Returns (Avoid Deep Nesting)

```php
// ✅ CORRECT: Early returns, flat structure
public function update(Market $market): void
{
    if (!auth()->check()) {
        abort(401);
    }

    if (!auth()->user()->can('update', $market)) {
        abort(403);
    }

    if (!$market->isActive()) {
        throw new MarketNotActiveException();
    }

    $market->update([...]);
}

// ❌ WRONG: Deep nesting
public function update($market)
{
    if (auth()->check()) {
        if (auth()->user()->can('update', $market)) {
            if ($market->isActive()) {
                $market->update([...]);
            }
        }
    }
}
```

### 4. Named Constants (No Magic Numbers)

```php
// ✅ CORRECT: Named constants
class MarketService
{
    private const MAX_OPTIONS = 10;
    private const MIN_OPTIONS = 2;
    private const DEFAULT_DURATION_DAYS = 30;

    public function validate(array $data): void
    {
        if (count($data['options']) < self::MIN_OPTIONS) {
            throw new ValidationException('Too few options');
        }
    }
}

// ❌ WRONG: Magic numbers
if (count($options) < 2) { } // What's 2?
if ($duration > 30) { } // What's 30?
```

### 5. Laravel Conventions

```php
// ✅ CORRECT: Follow Laravel patterns
Route::resource('markets', MarketController::class);
$this->authorize('update', $market);
DB::transaction(fn() => Market::create($data));

// ✅ CORRECT: Use Eloquent, not raw SQL
Market::where('status', 'active')->get();

// ❌ WRONG: Raw SQL with user input
DB::select("SELECT * FROM markets WHERE status = '$status'");
```

## Vue 3 (Options API) Style

### 1. Component Structure (Consistent Order)

```vue
<script lang="ts">
import { defineComponent, PropType } from 'vue';

// 1. Interfaces/types at top
interface Market {
    id: number;
    name: string;
}

// 2. Component definition
export default defineComponent({
    name: 'MarketCard',

    // 3. Components
    components: { Button },

    // 4. Props
    props: {
        market: {
            type: Object as PropType<Market>,
            required: true,
        },
    },

    // 5. Emits
    emits: ['update'],

    // 6. Data
    data() {
        return {
            isLoading: false,
        };
    },

    // 7. Computed
    computed: {
        statusLabel() {
            return this.market.status.toUpperCase();
        },
    },

    // 8. Watch
    watch: {
        'market.status'(newVal) {
            console.log('Status changed:', newVal);
        },
    },

    // 9. Lifecycle hooks
    mounted() {
        this.loadData();
    },

    // 10. Methods
    methods: {
        loadData() {
            // Implementation
        },
    },
});
</script>

<template>
    <div class="market-card">
        {{ market.name }}
    </div>
</template>

<style scoped>
.market-card {
    padding: 1rem;
}
</style>
```

### 2. Prop Types (ALWAYS Use PropType)

```vue
<script lang="ts">
// ✅ CORRECT: Typed props
import { PropType } from 'vue';

interface User {
    id: number;
    name: string;
}

export default {
    props: {
        user: {
            type: Object as PropType<User>,
            required: true,
        },
        status: {
            type: String as PropType<'active' | 'closed'>,
            default: 'active',
        },
    },
};

// ❌ WRONG: Untyped props
export default {
    props: {
        user: Object, // What properties does it have?
        status: String,
    },
};
</script>
```

### 3. Computed vs Methods

```vue
<script>
export default {
    data() {
        return {
            markets: [],
        };
    },

    computed: {
        // ✅ CORRECT: Use computed for derived state (cached)
        activeMarkets() {
            return this.markets.filter((m) => m.status === 'active');
        },

        totalVolume() {
            return this.markets.reduce((sum, m) => sum + m.volume, 0);
        },
    },

    methods: {
        // ✅ CORRECT: Use methods for actions
        async loadMarkets() {
            this.markets = await fetchMarkets();
        },
    },
};
</script>

<template>
    <!-- ✅ CORRECT: Reference computed property (not method call) -->
    <div>Active: {{ activeMarkets.length }}</div>

    <!-- ❌ WRONG: Calling method in template (not cached) -->
    <div>Active: {{ getActiveMarkets().length }}</div>
</template>
```

## TypeScript/JavaScript Style

### 1. Immutability (CRITICAL)

```typescript
// ✅ CORRECT: Create new objects
const updatedUser = {
    ...user,
    name: 'New Name',
};

const updatedArray = [...items, newItem];

// ❌ WRONG: Mutation
user.name = 'New Name'; // BAD!
items.push(newItem); // BAD!
```

### 2. Async/Await (Not Promises)

```typescript
// ✅ CORRECT: Async/await
async function fetchMarkets() {
    try {
        const response = await fetch('/api/markets');
        return await response.json();
    } catch (error) {
        console.error('Failed to fetch:', error);
        throw error;
    }
}

// ❌ WRONG: Promise chains
function fetchMarkets() {
    return fetch('/api/markets')
        .then((res) => res.json())
        .catch((err) => console.error(err));
}
```

### 3. Error Handling (ALWAYS)

```typescript
// ✅ CORRECT: Comprehensive error handling
async function submitForm(data: FormData) {
    try {
        const response = await api.post('/markets', data);

        if (!response.ok) {
            throw new Error(`HTTP ${response.status}`);
        }

        return response.json();
    } catch (error) {
        console.error('Form submission failed:', error);
        throw new Error('Failed to create market');
    }
}

// ❌ WRONG: No error handling
async function submitForm(data) {
    const response = await api.post('/markets', data);
    return response.json();
}
```

## File Organization

### Size Limits

- **PHP Classes**: 200-400 lines typical, 800 max
- **Vue Components**: 200-500 lines typical, 800 max
- **TypeScript Utilities**: 100-200 lines typical, 400 max
- **Methods/Functions**: <50 lines (extract if larger)

### Structure

```
MANY SMALL FILES > FEW LARGE FILES

✅ CORRECT: Feature-based organization
app/
├── Services/
│   ├── MarketService.php       (150 lines)
│   ├── OptionService.php       (120 lines)
│   └── ProbabilityService.php  (180 lines)

resources/js/
├── pages/Markets/
│   ├── Index.vue               (200 lines)
│   ├── Show.vue                (250 lines)
│   └── Create.vue              (300 lines)
├── components/
│   ├── MarketCard.vue          (150 lines)
│   └── OptionList.vue          (120 lines)

❌ WRONG: Monolithic files
app/Services/
└── MarketService.php           (2000 lines - too big!)
```

## Input Validation

### Laravel (Form Requests)

```php
// ✅ CORRECT: Dedicated Form Request
class StoreMarketRequest extends FormRequest
{
    public function rules(): array
    {
        return [
            'name' => ['required', 'string', 'max:200'],
            'description' => ['required', 'string', 'max:2000'],
            'options' => ['required', 'array', 'min:2'],
        ];
    }
}

// ❌ WRONG: Validation in controller
$request->validate([
    'name' => 'required|string|max:200',
    // ... many more rules
]);
```

## Code Quality Checklist

Before marking work complete:

### PHP/Laravel

- [ ] All methods have type declarations (PHP 8.2+)
- [ ] Controllers are thin (<100 lines)
- [ ] Business logic in services, not controllers
- [ ] Using Form Requests for validation
- [ ] Using Policies for authorization
- [ ] Eager loading to prevent N+1 queries
- [ ] No raw SQL with user input
- [ ] No magic numbers (use constants)

### Vue 3/TypeScript

- [ ] Props use PropType with interfaces
- [ ] Computed properties for derived state
- [ ] Methods for actions only
- [ ] No mutation (spread operator used)
- [ ] Async/await for promises
- [ ] Error handling on all async operations
- [ ] No console.log in production code

### General

- [ ] Code is readable and well-named
- [ ] Files are focused (<800 lines)
- [ ] No deep nesting (>4 levels)
- [ ] Early returns instead of nested ifs
- [ ] No hardcoded credentials or secrets
- [ ] Tests written for new features

---

**Stack**: Laravel 12 (PHP 8.2+) + Vue 3 Options API + Inertia.js + MySQL + TypeScript
